<h1><%= h(@community.name) %>: alerts</h1>

<div class="card muted">
  Everything this community's scripts have raised with <code>rubotty.alert</code>, newest first.
  A quiet alert is recorded here and nothing else happens. A loud one, written
  <code>rubotty.alert(text, "loud")</code>, is recorded the same way and rubotty also DMs this
  community's operators. A DM only reaches an operator on a platform rubotty can open one on, and
  only where they have messaged the bot before, so a loud alert that reached nobody says so in the
  How column rather than looking like it went out.
  Alerts are kept for <%= Rubotty::ControlPlane::Alerts::RETENTION / (24 * 60 * 60) %> days.
</div>

<% if @unseen.positive? %>
  <form class="inline" method="post" action="<%= request.script_name %>/communities/<%= h(@community.slug) %>/alerts/seen">
    <%= act_button("Mark all #{@unseen} seen", :manage_alerts, community: @community) %>
  </form>
<% end %>

<%= alerts_table(@alerts, community: @community,
                 empty: "No script in this community has raised an alert.") %>
